<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lorraine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lorraine is a region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, whose name derives from Lotharingia, the share of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a> after the division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. It was long contested between French and German rulers. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> annexed part of Lorraine together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> in 1871, and France regained it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lorraine.jpg" alt="Lorraine" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Niko67000 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carte_Lorraine_2018.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
